// An unsuffixed integer literal above INT32_MAX must mean the same number on every host.
//
// It did not. The grammar parsed these with `strtol`, whose `long` is 64-bit on Unix and 32-BIT ON
// WINDOWS (LLP64) — so a literal past 2147483647 SATURATED to LONG_MAX there, and the same source
// compiled to a different value depending on who built it.
//
// It surfaced in examples/webgpu, not in a test: `att.depthSlice = 4294967295` (WebGPU's
// DEPTH_SLICE_UNDEFINED) became 2147483647, wgpu rejected the render pass with "Depth slice was
// provided but the color attachment's view is not 3D", and the native triangle drew nothing on
// Windows while being correct on macOS. strtoll is 64-bit everywhere, so the narrowing to Int32Node's
// int32_t now wraps identically on all platforms — which is the whole point.
//
// The ASSIGNMENT path is the one that saturated; an initializer takes a different route through the
// emitter and always worked, which is most of why this went unnoticed for so long.
fn int32 main() {
    uint32 assigned = 0;
    assigned = 4294967295;
    if (assigned != 4294967295) { return 1; }

    uint32 hex = 0;
    hex = 0xFFFFFFFF;
    if (hex != 4294967295) { return 2; }

    return 42;
}
